From e9b4c41615f1ca615dd06ee10d05cbaac9382462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nieyin345 <nieyin0703@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:15:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sheets): reshell the chrome in Mcode's design tokens

Last of the five editors, same 54 shared chrome token values as the rest.

Sheets is the only one where the grid is a canvas: Univer paints it, and
upstream says so itself (App.tsx:1736): "Univer paints the grid on canvas, so
it can't follow the CSS tokens". That is fine and correct - cells, conditional
formats and chart palettes are document content, not chrome. The shell around
it (ribbon, name box, status bar, dialogs) is ExcelShell's own DOM and runs on
the shared tokens, which is what this file re-points.

The gate is the UA product token: Sheets' preload exposes window.desktopApi,
not desktop, so the Docs gate would never fire here.

91 app-private tokens stay untouched per the shared-token rule:
--sheets-paper, --sheets-chart-* and --chart-*, --sheets-pie-label-*,
--sheets-shape-*, --sheets-excel-blue / --excel-green*, --sheets-content-danger,
--sheets-validation-*, --univer-primary-600, and app-private chrome
(--sheets-statusbar-*, --sheets-scroll-thumb, --sheets-focus-ring,
--sheets-shadow-*).

o6-reshell-sheets-smoke: 42/42 in real Electron, four modes. Mutations: gate
removed 11 red, --surface reverted 2 red (sheets' ribbon reads --surface, not
--chrome-bg as pdf and slides do), import removed 12 red. Mutating --chrome-bg
leaves the suite green, which is correct and now documented: Sheets has zero
consumers for that token, and the suite prints the full list of shared tokens
this app does not consume (16) so the coverage set never drifts silently.

Two assertion bugs found and fixed while building this suite: the DOM check
assumed a .app container that Sheets does not have, and the "not window.desktop"
check used a substring test that window.desktopApi satisfies - it now uses a
word boundary.
